 @MuhdAkmalyoyoman90  It does look enjoyable at first, and first visit can be fun. The problem started after the Fox deal collapsed when Disney bought Fox. Originally SkyWorlds was meant to be a proper movie-driven, world-class park. After that fell through, a lot of the identity got watered down and replaced with safer, more generic stuff...

There are still some decent IPs left, but they’re not really fully used, so the park doesn’t feel as cohesive as places like Universal / Disneyland. On top of that, some of the big anchor rides like Mad Ramp Peak and the SFX coaster are still NOT open since launch, even though that one isn’t really Genting’s fault because the ride manufacturer went bankrupt.

So yeah, not saying SkyWorlds is shit, but it feels like we're paying international park prices for something that still runs more like... a local theme park. Untuk, first time okay, but not much replay value after that pun.

 @Don_Grifter it’s not the gambling that can be exclusive but the prestige treatment, access to clubs etc. It’s like the high rollers club where only people who could afford them be inside. 

But that’s the thing, these kind of clubs are usually not very profitable, they’d be lucky to not losing money. 

Just like all luxury car brands are owned by companies who sell mass market cars
